#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:36
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One cycle of a folio from plan to retirement, calling editing and the draft-to-publication path as call activities. folio-assistant — the content lifecycle end to end, one cycle of a folio. Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG. The <bootstrap.processes:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill that implements it; <cat-harness.processes:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared work plan in beans/."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:167
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the bean [bean-open]"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:53
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Opens and closes the cycle rather than running any of it: Task_Plan commits scope, team and artefacts before Lane_WorkPlan turns them into beans, and Task_Retire is reached only when Gateway_NextCycle finds nothing left to do — so this lane's second appearance is a judgement that the cycle is actually finished, not a step inside it."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:86
#. Diagram label
msgid "Plan scope, team, artifacts [content-plan]"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:184
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:168
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:52
#. Diagram label
msgid "Programme manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:78
#. Diagram label
msgid "Publication manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:174
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:156
