msgid "Scope the work, identify artifacts and actors, form the team, set the timeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:121
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "See draft-to-publication.bpmn."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:102
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "See editing-hci-validation.bpmn. Runs once per proposed change, not once per cycle."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:94
#. Diagram label
msgid "Seed the work plan [todo-manager]"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:180
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The corpus-wide check no single block's HCI validation gate can perform — cross-references, whole-folio build status, proof status and QA axes — sitting between the editor's accept and the publication manager's release, so a change that passed block-level review still has to clear folio-level checks before CallActivity_Publication ever runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:75
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The only reviewing this lane does happens AFTER publication, not before it: Task_Feedback triages what implementers and readers report on the LIVE folio, by severity and scope, and that triage — not a fresh review — is what Task_FeedbackBeans turns into the next cycle's work."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:79
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The single point in the cycle where the corpus becomes public: reached only after Task_Test has cleared the whole folio, and its own outcome is what Task_Feedback then collects reactions to — so whatever this lane calls out to in draft-to-publication.bpmn is the last gate before readers see anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:62
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The single re-entry point for every round the cycle contains — Gateway_NextCycle's 'yes' branch (H09) loops straight back here rather than to Task_Plan — so this lane runs once per proposed change, not once per cycle, and is where the accept decision on each of those changes is made before anything reaches the corpus-wide Task_Test."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:129
#. Diagram label
msgid "Triage published feedback [content-feedback]"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-lifecycle.bpmn:138
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Triaged feedback re-enters the work plan as beans, which is how the next cycle knows what it is for."
msgstr ""

